{
  "source": "scripts/color-taylor-script-cut-03.md",
  "wpm": 150,
  "gaps": {
    "line": 0.5,
    "paragraph": 1.2,
    "beat": 2.5
  },
  "lead": 3,
  "tail": 3,
  "lines": [
    {
      "id": "1.1",
      "beat": 1,
      "line": 1,
      "text": "Hey, I'm Taylor.",
      "start": 3,
      "end": 4.2,
      "gapBefore": 3
    },
    {
      "id": "1.1",
      "beat": 1,
      "line": 1,
      "text": "I'm a real human.",
      "start": 4.7,
      "end": 6.3,
      "gapBefore": 0.5
    },
    {
      "id": "1.2",
      "beat": 1,
      "line": 2,
      "text": "I'm also a user experience and product designer, and I'd like to show you something I've been working on.",
      "start": 7.5,
      "end": 15.1,
      "gapBefore": 1.2
    },
    {
      "id": "1.3",
      "beat": 1,
      "line": 3,
      "text": "It's called Color Taylor.",
      "start": 15.6,
      "end": 17.2,
      "gapBefore": 0.5
    },
    {
      "id": "2.1",
      "beat": 2,
      "line": 1,
      "text": "I've always been interested in, but struggled with, how red, green, and blue are used to make the colors on a display.",
      "start": 19.7,
      "end": 28.5,
      "gapBefore": 2.5
    },
    {
      "id": "2.2",
      "beat": 2,
      "line": 2,
      "text": "Hue, saturation, and brightness, and hue, saturation, and lightness are two approaches that make more sense to me, from working with color wheels for traditional art and design.",
      "start": 29.7,
      "end": 40.9,
      "gapBefore": 1.2
    },
    {
      "id": "2.3",
      "beat": 2,
      "line": 3,
      "text": "Our focus for this presentation will be HSB.",
      "start": 41.4,
      "end": 44.6,
      "gapBefore": 0.5
    },
    {
      "id": "2.4",
      "beat": 2,
      "line": 4,
      "text": "Color Taylor is meant to be a playground and educational tool for how RGB and HSB work together.",
      "start": 45.8,
      "end": 53,
      "gapBefore": 1.2
    },
    {
      "id": "2.5",
      "beat": 2,
      "line": 5,
      "text": "You see the relationships in real time, to help better understand how colors work on your display.",
      "start": 53.5,
      "end": 60.3,
      "gapBefore": 0.5
    },
    {
      "id": "2.6",
      "beat": 2,
      "line": 6,
      "text": "I'll just move myself out of the way.",
      "start": 61.5,
      "end": 64.7,
      "gapBefore": 1.2
    },
    {
      "id": "3.1",
      "beat": 3,
      "line": 1,
      "text": "The color editor on the right should be familiar to most people who have worked with creative tools.",
      "start": 67.2,
      "end": 74.4,
      "gapBefore": 2.5
    },
    {
      "id": "3.2",
      "beat": 3,
      "line": 2,
      "text": "The hexagon on the left is a different way of displaying the same information.",
      "start": 75.6,
      "end": 81.2,
      "gapBefore": 1.2
    },
    {
      "id": "3.3",
      "beat": 3,
      "line": 3,
      "text": "Hue is an angle that ranges from 0 to 360 degrees.",
      "start": 82.4,
      "end": 86.8,
      "gapBefore": 1.2
    },
    {
      "id": "3.4",
      "beat": 3,
      "line": 4,
      "text": "Red is 0...",
      "start": 88,
      "end": 89.2,
      "gapBefore": 1.2
    },
    {
      "id": "3.4",
      "beat": 3,
      "line": 4,
      "text": "green is 120...",
      "start": 89.7,
      "end": 90.9,
      "gapBefore": 0.5
    },
    {
      "id": "3.4",
      "beat": 3,
      "line": 4,
      "text": "and blue is 240.",
      "start": 91.4,
      "end": 93,
      "gapBefore": 0.5
    },
    {
      "id": "3.5",
      "beat": 3,
      "line": 5,
      "text": "The difference is that red, green, and blue each get their own direction on the hex, matching where they sit on the hue wheel.",
      "start": 94.2,
      "end": 103.8,
      "gapBefore": 1.2
    },
    {
      "id": "3.6",
      "beat": 3,
      "line": 6,
      "text": "And in between each of these we see combinations: yellow, cyan, and magenta.",
      "start": 105,
      "end": 110.2,
      "gapBefore": 1.2
    },
    {
      "id": "3.7",
      "beat": 3,
      "line": 7,
      "text": "Not to be confused with CMYK, which works differently and is for another time.",
      "start": 111.4,
      "end": 117,
      "gapBefore": 1.2
    },
    {
      "id": "4.1",
      "beat": 4,
      "line": 1,
      "text": "Let's take an orange as a reference point, 30 degrees.",
      "start": 119.5,
      "end": 123.5,
      "gapBefore": 2.5
    },
    {
      "id": "4.2",
      "beat": 4,
      "line": 2,
      "text": "When the hue is set to 30 degrees, I know that's going to be orange, because it's between red and yellow, and yellow is between red and green.",
      "start": 124.7,
      "end": 135.9,
      "gapBefore": 1.2
    },
    {
      "id": "4.3",
      "beat": 4,
      "line": 3,
      "text": "It's a combination of these two.",
      "start": 136.4,
      "end": 138.8,
      "gapBefore": 0.5
    },
    {
      "id": "5.1",
      "beat": 5,
      "line": 1,
      "text": "Adding saturation increases the distance between red, green, and blue.",
      "start": 141.3,
      "end": 145.3,
      "gapBefore": 2.5
    },
    {
      "id": "5.2",
      "beat": 5,
      "line": 2,
      "text": "Desaturating reduces the distance proportionally between these.",
      "start": 146.5,
      "end": 149.3,
      "gapBefore": 1.2
    },
    {
      "id": "5.3",
      "beat": 5,
      "line": 3,
      "text": "So we start to see blue become a bigger player, until eventually we've reached white at the center of the hex.",
      "start": 149.8,
      "end": 158.2,
      "gapBefore": 0.5
    },
    {
      "id": "5.4",
      "beat": 5,
      "line": 4,
      "text": "When all three are equal, there's no saturation, and you're left with gray.",
      "start": 159.4,
      "end": 164.6,
      "gapBefore": 1.2
    },
    {
      "id": "5.5",
      "beat": 5,
      "line": 5,
      "text": "Notice the hue didn't change.",
      "start": 165.8,
      "end": 167.8,
      "gapBefore": 1.2
    },
    {
      "id": "5.5",
      "beat": 5,
      "line": 5,
      "text": "Same arrangement, only the distance between color values moved.",
      "start": 168.3,
      "end": 171.9,
      "gapBefore": 0.5
    },
    {
      "id": "6.1",
      "beat": 6,
      "line": 1,
      "text": "Brightness is determined by the highest color value.",
      "start": 174.4,
      "end": 177.6,
      "gapBefore": 2.5
    },
    {
      "id": "6.2",
      "beat": 6,
      "line": 2,
      "text": "As we scale the brightness, the hue and saturation are maintained by scaling the RGB values proportionately to each other.",
      "start": 178.8,
      "end": 186.8,
      "gapBefore": 1.2
    },
    {
      "id": "6.3",
      "beat": 6,
      "line": 3,
      "text": "At a hundred percent brightness the hex is at its largest,",
      "start": 188,
      "end": 192.4,
      "gapBefore": 1.2
    },
    {
      "id": "6.4",
      "beat": 6,
      "line": 4,
      "text": "and lowering it shrinks the size of the hex.",
      "start": 192.9,
      "end": 196.5,
      "gapBefore": 0.5
    },
    {
      "id": "7.1",
      "beat": 7,
      "line": 1,
      "text": "We could use this orange and say we want six different tints of the same hue.",
      "start": 199,
      "end": 205.4,
      "gapBefore": 2.5
    },
    {
      "id": "7.2",
      "beat": 7,
      "line": 2,
      "text": "We can use HSB to come up with a bright desaturated orange, then go down the scale until we have a darker one.",
      "start": 206.6,
      "end": 215.8,
      "gapBefore": 1.2
    },
    {
      "id": "7.3",
      "beat": 7,
      "line": 3,
      "text": "This is really hinting at what a design system does.",
      "start": 217,
      "end": 221,
      "gapBefore": 1.2
    },
    {
      "id": "8.1",
      "beat": 8,
      "line": 1,
      "text": "If you want the classroom perspective, check out the equations section.",
      "start": 223.5,
      "end": 227.9,
      "gapBefore": 2.5
    },
    {
      "id": "9.1",
      "beat": 9,
      "line": 1,
      "text": "Now we can move on to the demo, which gives you an outline of some of the things to look for in the Color Taylor app.",
      "start": 230.4,
      "end": 240.8,
      "gapBefore": 2.5
    },
    {
      "id": "9.2",
      "beat": 9,
      "line": 2,
      "text": "It focuses on working with the tools that you feel most comfortable with.",
      "start": 241.3,
      "end": 246.5,
      "gapBefore": 0.5
    },
    {
      "id": "9.3",
      "beat": 9,
      "line": 3,
      "text": "You can find this demo the first time loading the app,",
      "start": 247.7,
      "end": 252.1,
      "gapBefore": 1.2
    },
    {
      "id": "9.4",
      "beat": 9,
      "line": 4,
      "text": "or from the question mark button at the top of the app.",
      "start": 253.3,
      "end": 258.1,
      "gapBefore": 1.2
    },
    {
      "id": "10.1",
      "beat": 10,
      "line": 1,
      "text": "Start with the sliders and controls you already know.",
      "start": 260.6,
      "end": 264.2,
      "gapBefore": 2.5
    },
    {
      "id": "10.2",
      "beat": 10,
      "line": 2,
      "text": "Moving one slider will highlight every other slider it affects.",
      "start": 265.4,
      "end": 269.4,
      "gapBefore": 1.2
    },
    {
      "id": "10.3",
      "beat": 10,
      "line": 3,
      "text": "Click the droplet button to switch between Source or Mixed colored sliders.",
      "start": 270.6,
      "end": 275.4,
      "gapBefore": 1.2
    },
    {
      "id": "10.4",
      "beat": 10,
      "line": 4,
      "text": "Click the tags button to show HTML colors on the hex.",
      "start": 276.6,
      "end": 281,
      "gapBefore": 1.2
    },
    {
      "id": "10.5",
      "beat": 10,
      "line": 5,
      "text": "Drag a handle on the hex and watch the RGB and HSB sliders follow.",
      "start": 282.2,
      "end": 287.8,
      "gapBefore": 1.2
    },
    {
      "id": "10.6",
      "beat": 10,
      "line": 6,
      "text": "Having fun is the goal of the tool.",
      "start": 289,
      "end": 292.2,
      "gapBefore": 1.2
    },
    {
      "id": "11.1",
      "beat": 11,
      "line": 1,
      "text": "If you use Figma, I've also made a Color Taylor plugin that you might like to check out.",
      "start": 294.7,
      "end": 301.9,
      "gapBefore": 2.5
    },
    {
      "id": "11.2",
      "beat": 11,
      "line": 2,
      "text": "That's Color Taylor!",
      "start": 303.1,
      "end": 304.3,
      "gapBefore": 1.2
    },
    {
      "id": "11.3",
      "beat": 11,
      "line": 3,
      "text": "Go play with it, and I hope it helps you see the relationship between RGB and HSB in a different light.",
      "start": 305.5,
      "end": 313.9,
      "gapBefore": 1.2
    },
    {
      "id": "11.4",
      "beat": 11,
      "line": 4,
      "text": "If it's useful, I'd like to hear from you.",
      "start": 315.1,
      "end": 318.7,
      "gapBefore": 1.2
    },
    {
      "id": "11.4",
      "beat": 11,
      "line": 4,
      "text": "Questions and feedback are welcome.",
      "start": 319.2,
      "end": 321.2,
      "gapBefore": 0.5
    },
    {
      "id": "11.5",
      "beat": 11,
      "line": 5,
      "text": "Thanks, see ya.",
      "start": 322.4,
      "end": 323.6,
      "gapBefore": 1.2
    }
  ],
